{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>But if after the Jubilee he consecrates.</b> And likewise if he consecrated it from the year of Jubilee and it remained in the hand of the treasurer, and this one comes to redeem it after the Jubilee." "<b>And the priest shall reckon to him the money according to the years that remain.</b> According to the reckoning; how so? He fixed its valuation for forty-nine years at fifty shekels — that is one shekel per year and one shekel extra for all of them, and the shekel is forty-eight pundion, which is one sela and one pundion per year, except that one pundion is lacking for all of them. And our Sages said that that pundion is a kalbon for small change, and the one who comes to redeem gives one sela and one pundion per year for the years that remain until the year of Jubilee (see Sifra; Arakhin 24)." "<b>And it shall be deducted from your valuation.</b> From the count of years from the year of Jubilee until the year of redemption."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:58.096265754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}